            <ArticleTitle>Absence attacks controlled by thalamic stimulation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>423-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Thalamic electrical stimulation in 3 patients alleviated chronic pain, absence attacks and spontaneously occurring delta and theta EEG discharges. It is suggested that diencephalic discharges may activate and/or lower the threshold for pain at the level of the diencephalon.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
